  "notes": "Built from the archived 2025-26 bulletin (bulletins.psu.edu/archive/2025-2026/undergraduate/colleges/liberal-arts/korean-ba/), fetched and raw-HTML-verified (semester subtotals 17.5+16+16+17.5+16+16+14.5+13.5 sum to the page's own stated 'Total Credits 127', matching KORBA-2026.json's total exactly). Structurally identical to the 2026-27 plan (KORBA-2026.json): LA 83 in Semester 1, a generic 'Second-Year Liberal Arts Seminar' slot in Semester 4 (the bulletin's own 'LA 283' code is unconfirmed, same convention KORBA-2026.json uses), and the same Semester 3 'KOR 120 or KOR 121N' pool -- confirmed via the archived 2025-26 course-description page (bulletins.psu.edu/archive/2025-2026/university-course-descriptions/undergraduate/kor/) that KOR 121 was already retitled 'KOR 121N: K-pop and Beyond' by this catalog year (the 'N' Inter-Domain suffix and retitling first appear in 2025-26, not before -- see KORBA-2022.json's notes for the pre-2025 plain 'KOR 121' form and its 2022-23/2023-24/2024-25 confirmation). The one real difference from 2026: KOR 450 ('Korean Cultures in Global Contexts') was still a real, listed 3cr course in the 2025-26 catalog (confirmed via the same archived course-description page) -- so this file's Semester 6 pool is the bulletin's real three-way 'KOR 450, 451, or 452', not 2026's two-way 'KOR 451, 452' (450 was discontinued sometime between the 2025-26 and 2026-27 catalogs; confirmed absent from the live 2026-27 course-description page, matching KORBA-2026.json's own finding). This addition doesn't change the credit total (still a 3cr slot either way) -- Total Credits 127 matches both years. KOR 498 remains excluded from the Semester 7 pool for the same variable-credit (1-9cr) reason as every other catalog year. Note: the archived 2025-26 page also separately publishes a second, distinct 'Korean, B.A. at Commonwealth Campuses' plan with different Semester 4/6 sequencing and a different 4-year total (125.5cr, not 127cr) -- not modeled here, consistent with every other KORBA-*.json file and this repo's University-Park-only scoping decision (docs/BRANCH_CAMPUS_FINDINGS.md); by the live 2026-27 catalog this Commonwealth-specific variant was dropped from the bulletin entirely, leaving only the single University Park plan modeled here and in KORBA-2026.json.",
